Log MQTT command failures that no client is waiting to hear about

An MQTT command gets no reply, so the log is its only feedback. main
logged every failed command as "Command failed: ..." from one deliver()
helper; v2.1 dropped that and only reads ctx.error when an HTTP reply is
waiting. Several failures therefore left no trace at all for MQTT
senders: a selector that matched nothing (the customer's speed sent
before its play had started), an empty selector, missing decoded
metadata, the concurrent-load limit, and a play superseded by stopall.

The scheduler now answers every request through deliver(): an HTTP
client gets the outcome as before; with nobody waiting, a failure is
logged once as WARN "Command failed: <reason>". Failures whose handler
already logs its own message (an unknown voice, an unavailable input, a
rejected talkback lease, a load or channel-alias error, a full audio
command ring, macro and parse errors) are recorded with
CommandCtx::fail_logged and are not logged a second time. HTTP logging
is unchanged.

docs/commands.md no longer calls an empty selector a silent no-op (it is
rejected: 400 over HTTP, a logged failure over MQTT), so its bugs.md
entry is gone; the troubleshooting guide says where to find a failed
MQTT command; the command-ordering bugs entry names the v2.1 log line.

Tests (the first, fourth and sixth failed before the change, logging
nothing): an MQTT speed that matches nothing logs "Command failed: No
sample matches the selector"; an MQTT voice_stop on an unknown voice
logs only its own warning; the same failing speed over HTTP logs
nothing and answers 404; an MQTT play over the load limit logs "Command
failed: Too many concurrent loads"; a failed MQTT load is logged once as
"Load failed"; an MQTT play superseded by stopall logs "Command failed:
Superseded by stopall/fadeall".

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings,
and a warning-free release build (RUSTFLAGS=-D warnings); fuzz suite 7
passed; broker-backed native suite (MQTTAUDIO_BROKER_TESTS=1, TLS CA
set) 981 passed, 0 failed, 7 device-gated ignored.

Prompts that led to this work:

- Decision after the design review: "Restore 'Command failed: ...'
  logging, as main has?" — "Yes (Recommended)": one ERROR/WARN line per
  failed MQTT command, HTTP unchanged.

